      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why return -ENOTTY here when compat_ioctl returns -ENOIOCTLCMD?",
      "revId": "a931a7e6579fe51b38214b5feec390fc5d4cea0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "878bd3ef_476b6988",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1390,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T19:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most compat_ioctl() implementations return -ENOIOCTLCMD.\n\nIt seems the reason for doing that is now obsolete, though, so I suppose we should just use ENOTTY for both.\n\n(ENOIOCTLCMD enabled fallback to the ioctl translation table defined in fs/compat_ioctl.c.  But that was removed in Linux v5.6, and this driver isn\u0027t using that table anyway.)",
      "parentUuid": "edd55f3e_d8d00d3d",
      "revId": "a931a7e6579fe51b38214b5feec390fc5d4cea0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7bee21f1_bab6405c",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1390,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T19:16:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the 5.4 kernel so returning -ENOIOCTLCMD in both cases might be safer than return -ENOTTY bot both.",
      "parentUuid": "878bd3ef_476b6988",
      "revId": "a931a7e6579fe51b38214b5feec390fc5d4cea0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ab505f8_6249ae9e",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1390,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T19:30:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s any safer, since this driver doesn\u0027t use the ioctl translation table in fs/compat_ioctl.c, and it *can\u0027t* because that wouldn\u0027t be compatible with GKI.  ENOTTY seems more future-proof since ENOIOCTLCMD is now obsolete, so I\u0027m leaning towards using ENOTTY.",
      "parentUuid": "7bee21f1_bab6405c",
      "revId": "a931a7e6579fe51b38214b5feec390fc5d4cea0b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
